+# JSON Results Output (`json-results`)
+
+## Overview
+
+The `json-results` output format exports **every executed check** — not just failed findings. Unlike the existing `json-ocsf` exporter (which skips file creation when there are no findings), `json-results` **always** generates a valid JSON file, even when all checks pass.
+
+This makes it suitable for building CSPM dashboards, compliance trend reports, posture scores, and historical analysis using **complete execution history**.
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# AWS scan
+prowler aws \
+  --output-formats json-results \
+  --output-directory ./output
+
+# Cloudflare scan
+prowler cloudflare \
+  --output-formats json-results \
+  --output-directory ./output
+```
+
+### Output Files
+
+| Provider   | Filename                  |
+|------------|---------------------------|
+| AWS        | `output/aws-results.json` |
+| Cloudflare | `output/cloudflare-results.json` |
+
+## JSON Schema
+
+Each record in the output array contains the following fields:
+
+| Field                  | Type    | Description                                      |
+|------------------------|---------|--------------------------------------------------|
+| `scan_id`              | string  | Unique scan identifier (e.g. `prowler-aws-<timestamp>`) |
+| `provider`             | string  | Cloud provider (`aws`, `cloudflare`, etc.)       |
+| `service`              | string  | Service name (e.g. `s3`, `waf`)                 |
+| `account_id`           | string  | Account / project ID                             |
+| `account_name`         | string  | Account display name                             |
+| `region`               | string  | Region or zone name                              |
+| `resource_uid`         | string  | Unique resource identifier (ARN, zone ID, etc.)  |
+| `resource_name`        | string  | Human-readable resource name                     |
+| `resource_type`        | string  | Resource type (e.g. `AWS::S3::Bucket`)          |
+| `check_id`             | string  | Prowler check ID                                 |
+| `check_title`          | string  | Check title                                      |
+| `check_description`    | string  | Check description                                |
+| `status`               | string  | Execution status: `PASS`, `FAIL`, `MANUAL`, `MUTED` |
+| `status_code`          | string  | Same as `status` (raw enum value)                |
+| `severity`             | string  | Severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `informational` |
+| `risk`                 | string  | Risk description                                 |
+| `categories`           | array   | Check categories (e.g. `["internet-exposed"]`)   |
+| `compliance_frameworks`| array   | Compliance frameworks matched (e.g. `["cis_3.0_aws"]`) |
+| `tags`                 | object  | Resource tags as key-value pairs                 |
+| `execution_time`       | number  | Execution time in seconds (0 if unavailable)     |
+| `timestamp`            | string  | ISO 8601 timestamp of the finding                |
+| `remediation`          | object  | Remediation details (see below)                   |
+| `documentation_url`    | string  | Link to check documentation                      |
+| `metadata`             | object  | Full check metadata (Pydantic `.dict()`)         |
+| `raw_result`           | object  | Raw check result data                            |
+
+### Remediation Object
+
+```json
+{
+  "recommendation_text": "Remove public access from the S3 bucket",
+  "recommendation_url": "https://hub.prowler.com/checks/aws/s3_bucket_public_read",
+  "code": {
+    "native_iac": "",
+    "terraform": "resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"example\" {\n  acl = \"private\"\n}",
+    "cli": "aws s3api put-bucket-acl --bucket my-bucket --private",
+    "other": ""
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## Example Output
+
+```json
+[
+  {
+    "scan_id": "prowler-aws-20250115T103000Z",
+    "provider": "aws",
+    "service": "s3",
+    "account_id": "123456789012",
+    "account_name": "production",
+    "region": "us-east-1",
+    "resource_uid": "arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket",
+    "resource_name": "my-bucket",
+    "resource_type": "AWS::S3::Bucket",
+    "check_id": "s3_bucket_public_read",
+    "check_title": "S3 Bucket Public Read Access",
+    "check_description": "Ensure S3 buckets are not publicly accessible",
+    "status": "PASS",
+    "status_code": "PASS",
+    "severity": "medium",
+    "risk": "Public read access to S3 buckets can expose sensitive data",
+    "categories": ["internet-exposed"],
+    "compliance_frameworks": ["cis_3.0_aws"],
+    "tags": {"Environment": "production"},
+    "execution_time": 0,
+    "timestamp": "2025-01-15T10:30:00+00:00",
+    "remediation": {
+      "recommendation_text": "Remove public access from the S3 bucket",
+      "recommendation_url": "https://hub.prowler.com/checks/aws/s3_bucket_public_read",
+      "code": {
+        "native_iac": "",
+        "terraform": "...",
+        "cli": "aws s3api put-bucket-acl --bucket my-bucket --private",
+        "other": ""
+      }
+    },
+    "documentation_url": "",
+    "metadata": {
+      "Provider": "aws",
+      "CheckID": "s3_bucket_public_read",
+      "CheckTitle": "S3 Bucket Public Read Access",
+      "ServiceName": "s3",
+      "Severity": "medium",
+      "ResourceType": "AWS::S3::Bucket",
+      ...
+    },
+    "raw_result": {"bucket_name": "my-bucket"}
+  }
+]
+```
+
+## Key Features
+
+1. **Always generates output**: The file is created even when there are zero findings (outputs `[]`).
+2. **Complete execution history**: Includes PASS, FAIL, MANUAL, and MUTED checks.
+3. **No breaking changes**: Existing output formats (`csv`, `json-ocsf`, `html`, `json-asff`, `sarif`) are untouched.
+4. **Direct serialization**: Uses Pydantic's `.dict()` for reliable, type-safe serialization.
+5. **Provider-agnostic**: Works with AWS, Cloudflare, and any other Prowler provider.
+
+## Integration with CSPM Dashboard
+
+The `json-results` format is designed for ingestion into your Cloudflare Worker + D1 database pipeline:
+
+1. **Worker**: Fetch the JSON file, parse it, and insert records into D1.
+2. **D1 Schema**: Store each record with indexes on `provider`, `account_id`, `service`, `check_id`, `status`, `timestamp`.
+3. **Dashboard Queries**:
+   - Posture score: `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM results WHERE status = 'FAIL'`
+   - Trends: `SELECT DATE(timestamp), COUNT(*) FROM results GROUP BY DATE(timestamp)`
+   - Compliance: `SELECT * FROM results WHERE compliance_frameworks LIKE '%cis_3.0_aws%'`
+
+## Comparison with Other Formats
+
+| Feature               | `json-results` | `json-ocsf` | `csv`  |
+|-----------------------|----------------|-------------|--------|
+| Always outputs file   | ✅ Yes         | ❌ No       | ❌ No  |
+| Includes PASS checks  | ✅ Yes         | ✅ Yes      | ✅ Yes |
+| Includes FAIL checks  | ✅ Yes         | ✅ Yes      | ✅ Yes |
+| Includes MANUAL       | ✅ Yes         | ✅ Yes      | ✅ Yes |
+| Schema                | Flat JSON      | OCSF        | Flat CSV |
+| Best for              | Dashboards     | SIEMs       | Spreadsheets |
+
